Package: AlphaSDM
Title: Species Distribution Modeling using Alpha Earth Embeddings
Version: 0.1.3
Authors@R:
    person("James", "Longo",
           email = "james.longo.birds@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Species distribution modeling on Google's Alpha Earth satellite
    embeddings, 64-dimensional dense vectors available at up to 10 m resolution
    anywhere on Earth, so no environmental layers need to be sourced or aligned
    locally. Provides tools to format occurrence records, train and
    cross-validate an ensemble of niche centroid and machine learning models,
    and export continuous habitat-suitability rasters. All data sampling, model
    training and prediction run server-side on Google Earth Engine, so the
    workflow scales to large datasets without local data handling.
